<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saudi Aramco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1933">1933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Aramco, Arabian American Oil Company</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saudi Aramco is the state oil company of Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and one of the largest companies in the world. It began as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> Arabian Standard Oil Company, formed in 1933 under a concession granted by King Abdulaziz, struck commercial oil at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dammam">Dammam</a> in 1938 and was renamed the Arabian American Oil Company in 1944. The Saudi government took full ownership by 1980, and a small share of the company was listed on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> stock exchange in 2019.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saudi-aramco.jpg" alt="Saudi Aramco" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saudi Press Agency (SPA) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Riyadh_Metro_(2024).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
